  "intro": {
    "sentences": [
      {
        "text": "Australian organisations and public agencies deploying autonomous AI agents must build governance and technical controls into systems from the start rather than relying on broad principles or after-the-fact reviews.",
        "cites": [
          "eea17d1397dbb4e5"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Frontier artificial intelligence firms operating in Australia face a wave of regulatory scrutiny and mandatory sharing of new models with safety and security agencies under a new joint committee report.",
        "cites": [
          "6e1f21ad7bac31cf"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "At the same time, organisations deploying agentic AI must adapt existing frameworks like ISO/IEC 42001 and NIST RMF by implementing layered safeguards and dynamic oversight to manage the unique risks of autonomous multi-step actions.",
        "cites": [
          "cc15fb5ac47a095d"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Furthermore, organisations operating AI and social media platforms in Australia face potential civil liability under new online safety laws following federal agreement to toughen the Digital Duty of Care legislation.",
        "cites": [
          "f3cf671205f88aff"
        ]
      }
    ],
